Project Details:
The project is a collaboration with Open AI and the Lenfest Institute as part of the super-customer initiative. 
Developed for external use by the Philadelphia Inquirer newsroom, it is a RAG-powered chatbot enabling reporters to quickly search and understand past Inquirer coverage to streamline their research process for new stories. 
It leverages a published archive of past Inquirer articles. 

Responsible AI (RAI): 
We add citation/reference to original articles into the generated answers to ground them for improved reliability/transparency.
We evaluate performance using metrics from Azure Foundry to ensure that the tool is effective and performs well for reporters. 
We also leverage the built in Azure Open AI responsible AI methods to scan the input and output of the tool. 
The main focus of this is to safeguard against prompt injections. 
Another common RAI category is harm (violence against self or others, sexual, etc.)
Due to the nature of news coverage, which contains violent or harmful content, we have chosen not to implement this category of RAI harm as it is a possible use case for reporters. 
However, we do want to safeguard against prompt injection using built in Azure Open AI methods 

Privacy: 
There is no privacy issue associated with the data we're storing and querying since this is a published archive of stories. 
However, we do want to log user queries to better understand the system performance so we will need to ensure that users consent to this.

